# CONTEXT DISCIPLINE

## Required reading — and nothing else

| # | Document |
|---|---|
| 1 | `docs/pipeline/P19-agent-operating-protocol.md` |
| 2 | `docs/ASSESSMENT-2026-07-30.md` |
| 3 | `docs/pipeline/README.md` |
| 4 | Your stage spec: `docs/pipeline/PXX-*.md` |

~2,000 lines total. That is the entire required reading for this project.
If you need more, **ask the user** — do not explore.

## Find your task

```bash
ls docs/pipeline/results/   # highest number = last completed stage; next one is yours
ls .local/                  # a PXX-* dir means that stage is in flight
```

## MUST

- Cite file paths — never paste whole files into a response.
- Reference `docs/METRICS.md` once for a metric definition; never re-define it.
- Use tables and bullets where they beat paragraphs.
- State which stage you are working on before implementing.

## NEVER

- Read `docs/pipeline/` stage specs other than your own.
- Reconstruct deleted history from `git show legacy/waves-w-bh` unless the user asks. It is 341,926 lines of the protocol that failed.
- Write a summary document. The only output document is `docs/pipeline/results/PXX.md`, one page, after the gate passes.
- Re-explain the assessment or the seven laws back to the user — cite the section.
